  "prompt": "Build v4 Posterize from photo-silk, its unchanged border and the exact 80/56/28px three-ring still at (60,35), (72,47), (86,61), with supplied #3A3A3A/#5A5A5A/#8A8A8A SVG payloads. On interaction, crossfade that illustrated still to the actual complete original photographic quantizer. Preserve both two/three-level RGB palettes, every source/output byte, the .18/.30 normalized radial bounds, smoothstep feather, .17 position response, .14 amount response and 32ms paint cap. Full keeps the complete photo-ocean composition and its original lens/readouts. Shell actions change levels, pin/release the lens and restore source; arrows move, Home centers, Space pins, L changes levels and Escape restores. Credit Milad Fakurian and Michael Benz. Use a 240×168 hero plane with the exact 200×150px image frame at (86,28) in the 372×264 stage: 14px corners, the supplied shadow and unchanged original SVG roots without width/height overrides. Full fields retain their original 368×268px geometry in a readable 400px-wide scroll camera. Prefix classes with rootClass and place controls in the shell. Preserve every original numerical model, typed buffer, image dataset, input rule, interruption and paint cap. Support scaled mouse coordinates, native keys and vertical touch scrolling, independent caller/viewport holds, queued intent and full cleanup. Keep the exact captured first pose until interaction, then use interruptible 150ms opacity feedback into the live model. Reduced motion keeps static feedback and disables ambient loops. Portable exports embed both Geist families, approved 800px photography and every photo credit/licence comment; local full views use their 1600px sources.",
